# cashcast actions (run each as `bin/cashcast …`; `--json` for the arguments)

- `bin/cashcast start`: set up, start the web app, refresh, and print what matters now (also: no command) (terminal only: it starts the web app you are using; run `bin/cashcast` in a terminal)
- `bin/cashcast stop`: stop the web app that `bin/cashcast` started (terminal only: it stops the web app you are using; run `bin/cashcast stop` in a terminal)
- `bin/cashcast weekly [--dry-run] [--balance BALANCE]`: the Sunday session in one run: fresh data, MoneyWiz, forecast, transfers, cards, charges, investing, tasks, and this week's moves (confirm: adds and fixes MoneyWiz rows, marks resolved tasks done and writes them to Reminders, Calendar and Notion (--dry-run changes nothing))
- `bin/cashcast help`: print the command overview
- `bin/cashcast init`: create your data folder
- `bin/cashcast import`: read the exports in your inbox
- `bin/cashcast status`: import, then the forecast summary
- `bin/cashcast forecast`: import, then the month-by-month forecast
- `bin/cashcast backtest`: import, then the last forecast vs actual, a backtest per line, and the spending methods learned
- `bin/cashcast numbers`: make an Apple Numbers copy of the forecast workbook
- `bin/cashcast totals`: totals per category and month
- `bin/cashcast first-error`: print the first unreadable export row (confirm: shows one raw row of your data on screen; agents: only with the owner's OK in chat and the agent:raw-row scope)
- `bin/cashcast columns`: header names and masked cell shapes of each inbox file (no values)
- `bin/cashcast holdings`: investments and crypto: quantity, cost base (ACB) and gains
- `bin/cashcast actions [--json]`: list every action with its arguments (for agents: --json)
- `bin/cashcast config {show|set}? KEY? VALUE?`: show the settings and where each value comes from, or set one
- `bin/cashcast users {list|add|adopt} NAME? [--province PROVINCE] [--display DISPLAY]`: list, add or adopt people (add: confirm (creates a person's data folder); adopt: confirm (moves the single-user data folder into a person's folder))
- `bin/cashcast consent {list|grant|revoke} {agent:aggregates|agent:raw-row|agent:strategy|cloud:sheets|cloud:notion|net:market-data|net:usage-counts|local:reminders|local:calendar|local:moneywiz|actions:browser|agent:browser-read|actions:api}?`: list, grant or revoke what may leave this computer (grant: terminal only; revoke: confirm (turns off a consent you granted); agents: never grant; give the owner the `consent grant SCOPE` command to run in a terminal)
- `bin/cashcast telemetry {status|on|off|send}? [--dry-run]`: opt-in anonymous usage counts to PostHog EU: status, on, off, send (--dry-run shows the body) (send: confirm (sends anonymous usage counts to PostHog EU (with consent net:usage-counts and a key)); agents: ask the owner in chat before `telemetry send` (without --dry-run) or `telemetry on`)
- `bin/cashcast strategy [--section SECTION] [--market]`: the full money plan (saved to out/strategy.md)
- `bin/cashcast net-total`: your net total (all you have minus all you owe), its trend, and the options ranked by what they add, inside your boundaries
- `bin/cashcast review`: the monthly review and checklist
- `bin/cashcast budget`: the budget section
- `bin/cashcast tax`: rates, room and tax moves
- `bin/cashcast rrsp`: this year's RRSP contributions (Sun Life and others) against your deduction limit
- `bin/cashcast alternatives`: cheaper cards, banks and services
- `bin/cashcast payments`: fees, interest and recurring payments
- `bin/cashcast spending`: spending checkup: more than usual, spend vs earn, interest and fees paid
- `bin/cashcast invest-plan`: ranked investment moves: gain ranges, evidence, risk, cost and do-nothing (override in [invest])
- `bin/cashcast invest [--market]`: long-term investing: core, placement and watchlist screen
- `bin/cashcast reminders {preview|sync}`: preview or sync your tasks to one Apple Reminders list (sync: confirm (writes your tasks to Apple Reminders); agents: preview here; the owner runs `sync` in Terminal (the sandbox blocks osascript))
- `bin/cashcast calendar {preview|sync}`: preview or sync your dated deadlines to one Apple Calendar (sync: confirm (writes your dated deadlines to Apple Calendar); agents: preview here; the owner runs `sync` in Terminal (the sandbox blocks osascript))
- `bin/cashcast tasks {list|resolve|verdict}? ID? {pass|fail}? [--reason REASON] [--source SOURCE] [--json]`: your open finance tasks: who does each (list), resolve what cashcast can and name every blocker (resolve), or record an agent check (verdict) (resolve: confirm (marks due tasks done that cashcast resolved itself (undo: changes undo ID)); agents: use /cashcast-tasks; report every BLOCKED task to the owner, never call it done)
- `bin/cashcast changes {list|show|done|undo}? ID?`: bank and card settings to change, ready for a browser session (agents: follow skills/bank-change; ask for a yes in chat right before each final click)
- `bin/cashcast transfers [--balance BALANCE]`: e-Transfers that bring each bank to its keep amount, from balances you read (daily limit, amounts quick to type)
- `bin/cashcast charges {check|find}? WORD?`: unexpected charges on every account: duplicate subscriptions, new recurring charges, price rises, charges after a pause; find WORD lists one merchant's charges
- `bin/cashcast grocery {items|show|best|stale|compare|save|fee|fees|order|orders|prefs|import}? NAME? [--items ITEMS] [--file FILE] [--from FROM] [--days DAYS] [--organic-premium ORGANIC_PREMIUM] [--delivery DELIVERY] [--free-over FREE_OVER] [--service SERVICE] [--pct-off PCT_OFF] [--max-off MAX_OFF] [--min-order MIN_ORDER] [--total TOTAL] [--note NOTE]`: grocery prices per store: best pack per 100 g, substitutes, store totals with fees and promos, orders and spend per month (agents: follow skills/grocery-cart; fill carts in the owner's Chrome, never check out or pay)
- `bin/cashcast cards {now}? [--balance BALANCE]`: which card to use now per spending category: cap used and left, reset date, rent charges, credit left
- `bin/cashcast optimize [--input INPUT]`: where new money goes to reach your target weights (you place the trades) (agents: show the plan; the owner places every trade)
- `bin/cashcast connectors {list|show} SERVICE?`: the services cashcast knows, and how to export from each
- `bin/cashcast action SERVICE ACTION_ID`: the safe steps for one service action, by risk (agents: money actions become reminders; never move money)
- `bin/cashcast api {balances|download|etrade-auth|record} SERVICE? TARGET? GID? [--set SET] [--currency CURRENCY]`: read balances or download exports through a service's API, or record balances read in the browser (etrade-auth: terminal only)
- `bin/cashcast fetch {plan|collect} [--all] [--minutes MINUTES]`: which exports are stale and how to get each (plan), or move new downloads into the inbox unopened (collect)
- `bin/cashcast sync {all|status|install|uninstall|sheets} DEST? [--allow-removals] RANGE?`: keep Reminders, Calendar and Notion in step (all, status, install hourly), or write the forecast to a Google Sheet (all: confirm (writes your tasks to Reminders, Calendar and Notion, and records the ones you ticked done); install: confirm (adds a LaunchAgent that runs sync all every hour); uninstall: confirm (removes the hourly sync); sheets: confirm (writes the forecast to your Google Sheet); agents: run `sync status`; the owner runs `sync all` and `sync install` in Terminal (the sandbox blocks osascript and launchctl))
- `bin/cashcast moneywiz {status|coverage|diagnose|categorize|sync|weekly|resync|edit|probe|categories} [--dry-run] {list|suggest|new|migrate|rollback}? [--name NAME] [--ops OPS] [--yes] [--ui] [--fixes] [--no-download] [--account ACCOUNT] [--archived ARCHIVED] [--from FROM] [--to TO] [--check] [--list] [--resend] [--record-since RECORD_SINCE]`: compare, sync and fix MoneyWiz against your exports (sync: confirm (adds rows to MoneyWiz); edit: confirm (changes rows in MoneyWiz))
- `bin/cashcast notion {import} SOURCE [--delete-source]`: import a Notion Markdown & CSV export, offline (import: confirm (imports documents (with delete_source it deletes the export)))
- `bin/cashcast web [--port PORT]`: run the web app in this terminal (terminal only: it is the web app itself)
- `bin/cashcast knowledge {check|list|propose|refresh} FILE?`: check, list, propose or refresh (live rates) the sourced facts
- `bin/cashcast paperwork VERB?`: citizenship steps, presence count and official sources, sealed on this Mac (terminal only) (terminal only: paperwork is private: run `bin/cashcast paperwork` in Terminal on this Mac)
- `bin/cashcast citizenship VERB?`: the guided citizenship application: answers, judges, proofs and the local evidence page (terminal only) (terminal only: the application holds ID numbers: run `bin/cashcast citizenship` in Terminal on this Mac)
exit 0
